# Mylonite CODEOWNERS
#
# This file is enforced. `main` is protected by a repository ruleset requiring
# code-owner review, so an entry here is a merge requirement rather than a
# suggestion. See GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# One line, deliberately. An earlier draft also listed the trust-base paths
# (workflows, gate-action/, .pre-commit-config.yaml, pyproject.toml, scripts/,
# .secrets.baseline, reference_targets/) individually. While a single owner
# holds the catch-all those entries enforce nothing the line below does not
# already enforce — they were prose in a config file, and prose belongs where
# contributors read it. That list now lives in CONTRIBUTING.md ("What we can and
# can't accept") and GOVERNANCE.md, which is also where the reason is given.
#
# Re-add the path scoping when a second maintainer joins: at that point the
# catch-all widens to the maintainer group, and those paths should keep naming
# the lead maintainer specifically. That is the moment the entries start
# meaning something. Note the ordering rule when you do — in CODEOWNERS the
# LAST matching pattern wins, which is the opposite of .gitignore.

